# Copy to `.env` and fill in. `.env` is gitignored.
#
# HOW THIS FILE IS READ. The CLI entry points (evals.agentdojo.runner and the
# scripts/ demos) load it from the repository root at startup. It never overrides
# a variable already exported in your shell, so an explicit export always wins.
# Nothing else reads it: the test suite does not, and `tests/conftest.py` strips
# provider keys from the environment for every non-costly test, so a test can
# never reach a real endpoint whatever is in here.
#
# You need exactly ONE key, and only to re-run the benchmark. Everything the
# README calls keyless - the attack demo, the playground, the retrieval eval, the
# statistics over committed results, the 763 tests - needs nothing from this file.

# --- The key the headline result was measured with -------------------------
# Groq, free tier, no credit card: https://console.groq.com
# 200,000 tokens/day, which is roughly 25-30 AgentDojo task runs.
GROQ_API_KEY=your-key-here

# --- Alternatives, both fully supported through flags ----------------------
# NVIDIA NIM (OpenAI-compatible), free tier: https://build.nvidia.com
#   --base-url https://integrate.api.nvidia.com/v1 --api-key-env NVIDIA_API_KEY
# Note: only meta/llama-3.1-8b-instruct responds quickly on the free tier, and an
# 8b model is NOT a valid security baseline - it scores ~0% attack success out of
# incapability rather than resistance. See results/README.md.
# NVIDIA_API_KEY=your-key-here
#
# Google AI Studio (Gemini), free tier: https://aistudio.google.com
#   --provider gemini
# Gemini 3.x needs its per-call thought_signature echoed back or every multi-turn
# tool loop fails; evals/agentdojo/gemini_llm.py handles that.
# GEMINI_API_KEY=your-key-here

# --- Not used by anything in this repository -------------------------------
# `anthropic` is a declared dependency but no provider is implemented for it.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=your-key-here
